### Create Named Temporary File in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/stebalien/tempfile/llms.txt

This Rust code creates a named temporary file with a filesystem path using NamedTempFile, writes and reads data, and auto-deletes on drop. It depends on tempfile and std::io. No specific inputs beyond creation; outputs include the file path and content. Useful for passing paths to other processes, with limitations on file persistence.

```rust
use tempfile::NamedTempFile;
use std::io::{Write, Read, Seek, SeekFrom};

fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    // Create named temporary file
    let mut file = NamedTempFile::new()?;

    // Get the path
    println!("Temporary file at: {:?}", file.path());

    // Write some data
    writeln!(file, "Named temporary file content")?;

    // Read it back
    file.seek(SeekFrom::Start(0))?;
    let mut buf = String::new();
    file.read_to_string(&mut buf)?;

    assert_eq!(buf, "Named temporary file content\n");

    // File automatically deleted when dropped
    Ok(())
}
```

