### Convert tempfile to path (Rust)

Source: https://context7.com/stebalien/tempfile/llms.txt

Converts a NamedTempFile to a TempPath, closing the file handle while maintaining automatic cleanup. Useful for passing paths to child processes without keeping the handle open.

```rust
use tempfile::NamedTempFile;
use std::io::Write;
use std::fs;

fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let mut file = NamedTempFile::new()?;
    writeln!(file, "Data for child process")?;

    // Close file handle but keep path
    let path = file.into_temp_path();

    // Path can now be passed to child processes
    // File handle is closed but cleanup still happens on drop
    println!("Temp path: {:?}", path.as_os_str());

    // Verify file still exists and is readable
    let contents = fs::read_to_string(&path)?;
    assert!(contents.contains("Data for child process"));

    // File deleted when path goes out of scope
    Ok(())
}
```

