### Multi-Process File Coordination with Locks in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Demonstrates coordinating access between multiple processes or threads using file locks. The `fs4` crate's `FileExt` trait provides `try_lock_exclusive` for acquiring locks with retries. This example uses `std::fs::OpenOptions` and `std::thread` for concurrency.

```rust
use fs4::fs_std::FileExt;
use std::fs::OpenOptions;
use std::io::Write;
use std::time::Duration;
use std::thread;

fn worker(id: usize) -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .read(true)
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("shared.log")?;

    // Try to acquire lock, retry if busy
    loop {
        match file.try_lock_exclusive() {
            Ok(true) => break,
            Ok(false) => {
                println!("Worker {} waiting for lock", id);
                thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100));
            },
            Err(e) => return Err(e),
        }
    }

    // Critical section - exclusive access guaranteed
    let mut file = file; // Make mutable
    writeln!(&mut file, "Worker {} writing", id)?;
    file.unlock()?;

    Ok(())
}

// Spawn multiple workers
let handles: Vec<_> = (0..5)
    .map(|id| thread::spawn(move || worker(id)))
    .collect();

for handle in handles {
    handle.join().unwrap()?;
}
```

