### Lock Contention Error Handling in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Shows how to handle lock contention errors specifically, using `fs4::lock_contended_error` to identify platform-specific errors. This allows for robust error management when dealing with concurrent file access. It utilizes `std::fs::OpenOptions` and `FileExt` from `fs4`.

```rust
use fs4::{fs_std::FileExt, lock_contended_error};
use std::fs::OpenOptions;
use std::io::ErrorKind;

let file1 = OpenOptions::new()
    .read(true)
    .write(true)
    .create(true)
    .open("test.txt")?;

let file2 = OpenOptions::new()
    .read(true)
    .open("test.txt")?;

file1.lock_exclusive()?;

// Check for specific lock contention error
match file2.try_lock_shared() {
    Ok(false) => println!("Lock contended - file is locked"),
    Ok(true) => println!("Lock acquired"),
    Err(e) if e.kind() == lock_contended_error().kind() => {
        println!("Detected lock contention error");
    },
    Err(e) => eprintln!("Other error: {}", e),
}

file1.unlock()?;
```

