### Asynchronous File Locking with Tokio

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Shows asynchronous file locking and allocation using `fs4::tokio::AsyncFileExt` with `tokio::fs::File`. Lock operations are synchronous, but methods like `allocate` and `allocated_size` are asynchronous. Requires the `tokio` runtime and `tokio-fs` integration. Includes `unlock_async` for convenience in async contexts.

```rust
use fs4::tokio::AsyncFileExt;
use tokio::fs::OpenOptions;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .read(true)
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("async_data.txt")
        .await?;

    // Lock operations are synchronous (no .await)
    file.lock_exclusive()?;

    // Async operations
    file.allocate(1024 * 1024).await?; // Pre-allocate 1MB
    let size = file.allocated_size().await?;
    println!("Allocated size: {} bytes", size);

    // Async unlock for convenience in async contexts
    file.unlock_async().await?;

    Ok(())
}
```

