### fs-err Integration for Enhanced Error Reporting in Rust

Source: https://context7.com/al8n/fs4-rs/llms.txt

Integrates `fs4` with `fs-err` for enhanced error reporting, including path information in error messages. This applies to both synchronous and asynchronous (tokio) operations. It requires `fs4`, `fs-err`, and optionally `tokio`.

```rust
// With fs-err v3
use fs4::fs_err3::FileExt;
use fs_err::OpenOptions;

let file = OpenOptions::new()
    .write(true)
    .create(true)
    .open("data.txt")?;

file.lock_exclusive()?;
file.allocate(1024)?;
file.unlock()?;

// With fs-err v3 tokio
use fs4::fs_err3_tokio::AsyncFileExt;
use fs_err::tokio::OpenOptions;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let file = OpenOptions::new()
        .write(true)
        .create(true)
        .open("async_data.txt")
        .await?;

    file.lock_exclusive()?;
    file.allocate(2048).await?;
    file.unlock_async().await?;

    Ok(())
}
```

